    {
      "value": {
        "start": "45",
        "end": "45",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 130,
        "text": "Gen Z like Luis entered adulthood tagged by a global pandemic, learning in solitary confinement and living on a terminal timeline.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "39B84CAECE",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "46",
        "end": "46",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 62,
        "text": "I asked Luis, “How does the world taste?” And he said, \"Spicy.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "BF556DAEB3",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "47",
        "end": "47",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 45,
        "text": "Climate tastes a lot spicier than it used to.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C98B7311C7",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 120,
        "text": "It's demotivating when people are telling you, ’Dude, all the carbon’s already in the atmosphere at irreversible levels.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "ADD6AFEFA6",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "49",
        "end": "49",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 185,
        "text": "You know money-hungry people aren’t going to stop being money-hungry.’” Luis is the first Sarabia to attend Stanford University, and for Luis, life is as simple and as complex as tacos.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "52DCF86B3C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "50",
        "end": "50",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 69,
        "text": "He told me, \"I'm so proud my culture created something so delicious.\"",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "499A0E0BD7",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "51",
        "end": "51",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 62,
        "text": "For Luis, tacos are family, tacos are friends, tacos are hope.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "2136EEB144",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "52",
        "end": "52",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 87,
        "text": "Gen Z are carrying hot sauce in their backpack to make bland, no-change food palatable.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "32F16CAB34",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "53",
        "end": "53",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 67,
        "text": "They're our hot sauce to tell us they're just at the starting line.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "INCOMPLETE"
        ]
      },
